yle=\"color:#000\"> of </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Approximation</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>  RMSEA                                          </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">90</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Percent</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Confidence</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Interval</span><span style=\"color:#000\">          </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.000</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  P</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">value RMSEA </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.05</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                          </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Standardized</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Root</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Mean</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Square</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Residual</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>  SRMR                                           </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Parameter</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Estimates</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Information</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                                 </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Expected</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Standard</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Errors</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                             </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Standard</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>My problem is that I do not understand why I get output showing (if i understand this correctly) that my model is fully saturated. My total number of free parameters is 55 (10*(10+1)/2) and I estimate 51 parameters: 5*5 paths from X and C1-4 to M1-2 and Y1-3; 2*3 paths from M1-2 to Y1-3, 10 variances of the observed vars and 10 covariances I modeled myself. Hope to hear from the experts where I am going wrong :)</div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;lavaan&quot; group.<br></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div>"
